      <Docs>
        <param name="response">The source response to snapshot.</param>
        <summary>
            Creates an immutable deep copy of the <see cref="T:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Responses.Models.ResponseObject" /> via
            <see cref="T:System.ClientModel.Primitives.ModelReaderWriter" /> round-trip serialization.
            </summary>
        <returns>
            A new <see cref="T:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Responses.Models.ResponseObject" /> instance that is fully independent of the original.
            Mutations to the original do not affect the snapshot and vice versa.
            </returns>
        <remarks>
            Uses <see cref="M:System.ClientModel.Primitives.ModelReaderWriter.Write(System.Object,System.ClientModel.Primitives.ModelReaderWriterOptions,System.ClientModel.Primitives.ModelReaderWriterContext)" /> and
            <see cref="M:System.ClientModel.Primitives.ModelReaderWriter.Read``1(System.BinaryData,System.ClientModel.Primitives.ModelReaderWriterOptions,System.ClientModel.Primitives.ModelReaderWriterContext)" />
            which leverage the TypeSpec-generated <see cref="T:System.ClientModel.Primitives.IPersistableModel`1" /> implementation.
            This guarantees all properties — including polymorphic <see cref="T:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Responses.Models.OutputItem" /> subtypes,
            <see cref="T:System.BinaryData" /> union fields, and additional binary data properties — are
            fully serialized and deserialized into an independent object graph.
            </remarks>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
